Mathematical extraction from pyCM1.1.8, Matthew J. Roy (2017), GPL3;
original copyright/license notice is preserved in LICENSE. The exact paper
repository and source qualifications are identified in maintainer provenance.

This package explicitly implements the eight-node elastic acquisition operator,
surface fit, displacement elimination and contour stress reconstruction locally.
No original finite-element/domain reconstruction library is required at runtime.

The source Gauss-to-node postprocessor fails independently known linear-stress
tests. The qualified method evaluates inverse shape interpolation in actual
native quadrature order. Original deficient results remain separately identified.
The proper second-anchor constraint fixes only the stress-invariant rigid gauge.

The real observations are the author's published registered/averaged CMM record.
The associated original raw-face dataset is CC-BY4.0; a separate redistribution
grant for the repository's higher-precision processed MAT record is not explicit.
The software GPL notice is not asserted to be a separate data license. Local
research provenance is retained; no external publication/upload is performed.

Only cut-face normal restoration stress is reconstructed. Interior relaxation
stresses are diagnostics, not the original interior residual-stress tensor.
The physical pre-cut release-sign calibration is not independently supplied.
